{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And they asked of them and they despoiled, etc.</b> The meaning is: because HaShem granted the people favor in the eyes of the Egyptians, and because of this the Egyptians lent to them against their will — and because of this they justified the matter, for their intention was not to depart permanently; had that been so, they would have sought to take from them to gain more, and thereby ״they despoiled Egypt.״ Now, the one who reflects on this matter will see that a person's own deed is repaid to him (Berakhot 9a) — for because Israel cherished the matter of the Exodus and did not concern themselves with the enjoyment of wealth, that very thing was the cause that they [the Egyptians] went to extraordinary lengths to give abundantly, and their merit stood for them."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:16.062520635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}